# TI_LM5164DDAR — component wrapper: local KiCad symbol + footprint, LCSC pinned
# in properties (feeds the JLC BOM/CPL fields).
#
# 100 V, 1 A SYNCHRONOUS buck converter, SO-8 with exposed pad. The compact-rail
# alternative to the SY8513FCC for boards where area and height are the binding
# constraints (Ben, 2026-09-05, after reviewing how the N17's TI rails stayed
# small). Datasheet SNVSAU4A read 2026-09-05; the numbers that matter:
#
#   * INTEGRATED synchronous rectifier, 0.34 ohm. No external Schottky at all,
#     which removes an SMB from the cell and the heat that went with it.
#   * Switching to 1 MHz with a 50 ns minimum on-time (the SY8513 is capped at
#     500 kHz with a 180 ns floor). That is what lets the inductor drop from
#     3.0 mm tall to 2.0 or less - at 1 MHz a 48 V to 5 V rail runs 0.20 A of
#     ripple against 0.68 A at 300 kHz.
#   * Junction range -40 to +150 C. The SY8513's RECOMMENDED range is an
#     AMBIENT of -40 to +85 C, and this ecosystem's sealed node is designed to
#     100 C, so the incumbent is outside its range in that application.
#   * COT control with an internal bias regulator and boot diode: the external
#     set is inductor, input caps, output caps, a 2.2 nF BST cap, the on-time
#     resistor and the feedback divider. Ten parts against the SY8513 cell's
#     sixteen.
#   * On-time is programmed by RON and compensated for input voltage, so
#     fsw = Vout / (400e-9 * RON[kohm]) and holds across the 48 V bus's
#     56-58 V chopper window.
#
# LIMIT: 1 A output. It does not serve the Flyweight's servo rails or the CNC
# Expansion's 2 A IO rail - those keep the SY8513, or take an LM5146 controller
# driving the 100 V FET already in the bridge BOM.
# THERMAL TO VERIFY AT BRING-UP: at 24 V and 0.7 A the part passes ~17 W and
# dissipates ~1 W; RthJA is 41.1 C/W on a JEDEC board, so the junction sits near
# 141 C at a 100 C ambient against the 150 C limit. It wants the lid face and a
# generous pad pour.
# Pinned 2026-09-05: LCSC C477928, Extended, 3087 in stock, $1.98.

GND = io("GND", Ground, optional = True)
VIN = io("VIN", Net, optional = True)
EN = io("EN", Net, optional = True)
RON = io("RON", Net, optional = True)
FB = io("FB", Net, optional = True)
PGOOD = io("PGOOD", Net, optional = True)
BST = io("BST", Net, optional = True)
SW = io("SW", Net, optional = True)

Component(
    name = "TI_LM5164DDAR",
    footprint = File("TI_LM5164DDAR/SO-8_L4.9-W3.9-P1.27-LS6.0-BL-EP.kicad_mod"),
    symbol = Symbol("TI_LM5164DDAR/LM5164DDAR.kicad_sym"),
    prefix = "U",
    part = Part(mpn = "LM5164DDAR", manufacturer = "Texas Instruments"),
    properties = {"LCSC": "C477928", "MPN": "LM5164DDAR"},
    pins = {
        "GND": GND,
        "VIN": VIN,
        "EN/UVLO": EN,
        "RON": RON,
        "FB": FB,
        "PGOOD": PGOOD,
        "BST": BST,
        "SW": SW,
        "EP": GND,
    },
)
